  "verbalization": "Scandoside is shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which is a known target of multiple compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, 3-Bromo-4-(2,3-Dibromo-4,5-Dihydroxybenzyl)-5-Methoxymethylpyrocatecol, and Lindoldhamine. All these compounds share a common target of Neuropilin-2, suggesting that Scandoside may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the modulation of Neuropilin-2. The evidence indicates that Scandoside may act as a modulator of SNU-387, which in turn affects Neuropilin-2. The integration of these pathways suggests that Scandoside may influence Neuropilin-2 through a shared target, potentially via a mechanism involving the regulation of SNU-387. The final scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact mechanism of action.",
